      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"SYS_RST\" is an input signal to the SOC when asserted expected to triggers reset but PLT_RST is output from SOC indicates CPU reset.\n\nAs per PDG Document:\nThe Processor asserts PLTRST# to reset devices on the platform (e.g.,\nSIO, LAN etc.). Asserted during power-up and when S/W initiates a\nhard reset sequence through the Reset Control register.\n\nIf there are other scenarios ex: AP/OS hangs/asserts due to which CPU reset is triggered monitoring the \"SYS_RST\" signal will not help.",
